  "texts": {
    "preamble": "B Nagarjuna vs State Of Andhra Pradesh on 15 October, 2019 Author: U. Durga Prasad Rao Bench: U. Durga Prasad Rao Hon'Ble Sri Justice U. Durga Prasad Rao Criminal Petition No.6133 of 2019 Order:",
    "facts": "The petitioners/A3 & A4 seek to quash the proceedings against them in Crime No.573 of 2019 of Gajuwaka Police Station, Visakhapatnam, registered for the offences under Sections 188, 273, 328 r/w 34 IPC and Section 59 of the Food Safety and Standards Act (for short, 'FSS Act'). 2. The allegations against the petitioners briefly are that on 02.10.2019 at 18.00 hours, the complainant while conducting inspection of vehicles, intercepted the auto bearing registration No.AP 31TF 3170 and on enquiry the petitioners-A3 & A4 confessed that they were transporting the banned tobacco products on the instructions given by A1 & A2 and hence, seized the same and registered a case in Crime No.573 of 2019 of Gajuwaka Police Station, Visakhapatnam for the offences stated supra. 3.",
    "arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners, while denying the FIR allegations, would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "petitioner_arguments": "Learned counsel for petitioners, while denying the FIR allegations, would submit that even if the prosecution case is accepted to be true, tobacco products would not fall within the definition of Section 3(j) of FSS Act and therefore, the Police are not authorized to register the crime, investigate and file charge sheet and therefore, registration of the FIR is contrary to the provisions of FSS Act.",
    "respondent_arguments": "",
    "other_lawyer_arguments": ""
  },
